WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.040
Today's Designed by Drew viewer thinks he's here

2
00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:07.040
for some design advice and has no idea that we actually

3
00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.650
have a brand new room waiting for him.

4
00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:14.300
So let's meet Chris who went from being homeless

5
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:19.300
four years ago to now, being the proud homeowner

6
00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:23.105
of a four bedroom house.

7
00:00:23.105 --> 00:00:24.272
Oh!
I know!

8
00:00:25.653 --> 00:00:27.244
(applause)

9
00:00:27.244 --> 00:00:28.494
Check out this.

10
00:00:30.434 --> 00:00:32.290
(gentle urban music)

11
00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:34.080 line:15%
Hi, Drew, my name is Chris.

12
00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.870 line:15%
I'm 24 years old, and I live in Williamstown, New Jersey.

13
00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.610
I fell on hard times in 2016.

14
00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:41.330
I was a freshman in college

15
00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:44.330
and I was working full-time and going to school full time.

16
00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.410
And I had to pay for school out of pocket.

17
00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:49.660
Unfortunately, when I was 18, I became homeless

18
00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:51.710
and I was living out of my car for,

19
00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:53.520
it was like six to eight months.

20
00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.740
And it got to a point where I had literally pennies

21
00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:56.573
in my account.

22
00:00:56.573 --> 00:00:58.720
I just decided to turn my life around.

23
00:00:58.720 --> 00:00:59.860
I didn't like where I was

24
00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:01.840
and I wanted to be in a different place.

25
00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:05.120
The next day, I must've applied for over 2000 jobs.

26
00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.810
Eventually I got my first real job selling mattresses.

27
00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:09.597
I was still homeless.

28
00:01:09.597 --> 00:01:11.138
I actually was able to go back

29
00:01:11.138 --> 00:01:12.720
to school and I went to an online coding academy

30
00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.490
and I got my first engineering job

31
00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:16.120
and then a second one.

32
00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:18.400
But I decided that I wanted to buy a house

33
00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:20.360
because I wanted to have a place

34
00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:23.290
for my children to grow up and have a stable place

35
00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:25.360
and a yard that's big enough for them to play

36
00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.390
and somewhere where they can actually call home.

37
00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:28.730
So I bought my house.

38
00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:30.620
I was able to save up enough for it.

39
00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:33.460
My next goal is just making my house a home

40
00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.080
for me and my kids.

41
00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:36.900
I truly believe in taking life

42
00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.620
by the horns and manifesting your own happiness.

43
00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:43.243
I believe that no obstacle is too great.

44
00:01:43.243 --> 00:01:45.696
(applause)

45
00:01:45.696 --> 00:01:48.240
Chris is here now.

46
00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.720
Hi, Chris, how are you?

47
00:01:51.347 --> 00:01:54.203
I'm okay, thank you for having me.

48
00:01:54.203 --> 00:01:57.500
May I ask, how is everything

49
00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:00.713
for you now in your new home?

50
00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:02.780
It's great.

51
00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:07.281 line:15%
I'm used to living in apartments where it's kind of cramped

52
00:02:07.281 --> 00:02:09.590 line:15%
and you know, maybe one bedroom, maybe a few

53
00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:10.900
hundred square feet or something.

54
00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:12.720
And now I have this pretty decent

55
00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:14.820
sized house that I'm really proud of.

56
00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:17.110
And I love just being able to wake up

57
00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:19.870
seeing all the things that I've built, put together,

58
00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:21.600
and that I am still building for.

59
00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.080
So it's great.

60
00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.520
This was the first time in my life

61
00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:27.170
where I was actually happy about something that I did.

62
00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:29.400
And I think I needed that to help me be proud

63
00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:32.990
of myself and see that what I did do was something great.

64
00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:35.690
What was it about this house, may I ask,

65
00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:38.740
that spoke to you and said, this is the dream.

66
00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:40.683
It was the perfect foundation.

67
00:02:40.683 --> 00:02:44.220
I was thinking of it, of what I can turn this into.

68
00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:45.630
And it had everything laid out.

69
00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:47.300
I loved how big the yard was

70
00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.900
because I want my kids to be able to run around

71
00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:53.680
and have a place to play and, you know, hurt themselves

72
00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:54.905
and come to me.

73
00:02:54.905 --> 00:02:56.525
(laughter)

74
00:02:56.525 --> 00:02:59.810
You know, and have friends come over and have barbecues,

75
00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:01.370
have birthday parties in a place

76
00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:03.430
where they can always call home.

77
00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:05.390
I saw the big backyard and I was like,

78
00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:06.760
that's definitely something that I want.

79
00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:08.721
I saw the rooms that it had.

80
00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:11.120
I saw the basement that I was turning

81
00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:12.700
into a theater, because I went to the attic,

82
00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:15.380
which I was turning into a library slash art room.

83
00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:18.100
It's the foundation that I wanted that said,

84
00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:20.430
this is exactly what I need to get started

85
00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:23.400
to make it the dream house that I want it to be.

86
00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.730
Well, that is so well put.

87
00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:28.170
And you have two beautiful children,

88
00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:33.170
your three-year-old son Carter, and Xavier is on the way.

89
00:03:36.156 --> 00:03:39.930
Well, then I think there is something important

90
00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:41.820
that we're gonna need to do.

91
00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:46.820
And I was wondering if I could involve myself

92
00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:51.590
in your new son's room, Xavier?

93
00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:52.940
Absolutely, absolutely.

94
00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:53.773
Please do.

95
00:03:54.743 --> 00:03:55.630
(applause)
Okay, good.

96
00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:59.560
So you haven't started on your son's nursery, right?

97
00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:01.890
Right, it's a blank slate.

98
00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:03.980
Thank you for letting me be a part of this.

99
00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:08.220
This was your son's room as it is now.

100
00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:11.433
And here is what I would like to do with it, ta-da!

101
00:04:13.096 --> 00:04:15.346
(applause)

102
00:04:18.397 --> 00:04:19.230
Oh wow!

103
00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:25.420
Which, basically Chris, I kind of already went and did.

104
00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:27.143
I hope that's okay.

105
00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:30.930
That's completely fine with me.

106
00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:34.650
Okay, this is Xavier's new nursery and you are

107
00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:39.030
gonna get every single thing that you see in here.

108
00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:44.030
And we were lucky enough to work with Pottery Barn Kids,

109
00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:47.070
one of my favorite stores

110
00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:50.240
and we just had your baby boy in mind.

111
00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:55.240
And here is three design tips that we really got into.

112
00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:56.540
All right.

113
00:04:56.540 --> 00:05:01.540
We thought about using bins for shelving

114
00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:04.560
because you can kind of quickly take stuff in there,

115
00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:06.180 line:15%
throw it in there, put it back.

116
00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:09.403 line:15%
And it'll just look really neat and tidy.

117
00:05:09.403 --> 00:05:12.920 line:15%
Also, we have a toy chest here

118
00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:15.090
and those really, really help and this is a really

119
00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:20.090
great one that doesn't allow any finger accidents to happen.

120
00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:24.363
Also, I did wanna bring a little color into it.

121
00:05:24.363 --> 00:05:28.030
This is actually a Flower Home piece of artwork

122
00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:31.170
and we kind of went with like an animal jungle theme.

123
00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:35.201
And the reason I chose this crib

124
00:05:35.201 --> 00:05:38.313
is because, I'll show you.

125
00:05:40.216 --> 00:05:41.410
When you bend over it,

126
00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:44.460
there's actually a dip for your waist.

127
00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:48.860
And I can't tell you how many times I have jabbed my ribs

128
00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:51.990
my xiphoid process, my solar plexus

129
00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:54.270
trying to get that baby in and out.

130
00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:57.210
Whoever figured this moment out,

131
00:05:57.210 --> 00:06:01.160
on behalf of every parent and their chests, thank you.

132
00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.110
I so appreciate that.

133
00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:06.150
All right, now I like this chair

134
00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:09.330
because I specifically placed it in this area

135
00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:12.770
of your room because this chair is the power position.

136
00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:16.670 line:15%
It can see the door that you enter

137
00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:19.740 line:15%
because I wanted who's ever sitting in this chair

138
00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:22.880 line:15%
with little Xavier to feel like whoever is coming in

139
00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:25.280
and out, you can be seen directly.

140
00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:28.830
And we did these decals on the walls so

141
00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:33.830 line:15%
that you could feel that fun jungle animal motif

142
00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:38.390 line:15%
and keep it going with the rug and the walls.

143
00:06:38.390 --> 00:06:40.270 line:15%
But we tried to keep it delicate

144
00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:44.550 line:15%
and not sort of overdo every space on the wall.

145
00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:46.510 line:15%
So this is it.

146
00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:49.030
I can not say thank you enough.

147
00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:51.740
You just blew my mind and this is probably

148
00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:53.882
the nicest thing somebody ever done for me.

149
00:06:53.882 --> 00:06:55.460
Thank you so much.

150
00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:56.560
I really appreciate it.

151
00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:59.290
Words can't express my gratitude.

152
00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:00.410
Thank you, Chris.

153
00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:03.250
And thank you to Carter and almost welcome

154
00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:06.340
to Xavier and we'll check back in

155
00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:09.079
and see how everything is going with you.

156
00:07:09.079 --> 00:07:11.746 line:15%
(upbeat music)

